          "source_text_sha256": "09b7214b8dbcf0a1d8ba9f5dfcbd71b8bb5679596a98807994deb3aba92b86b1",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On Saturday, July 4, 2009, around 11:40 PM, from his home, a witness observed the silent passage of a bright disk in the sky for 2 to 3 seconds. The movement was straight-line and at a very high speed along a trajectory from Bordeaux to Perpignan. No other witnesses were reported for this phenomenon. This case of observation of a very bright disk crossing the sky in a few seconds suggests an atmospheric reentry of a meteorite. However, the witness does not note a green or yellow streak, as expected in such cases. It could be assumed that the witness's night-time visual acuity is not very good due to his age. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of an atmospheric reentry of a meteoroid (meteorite).",
          "translation_text_sha256": "2dd4467de52948ad4ea65735e1eebccd115230bfcd3a50ea3439bc9db9a27392"
        }
